analysisWe need to produce assert statement for comment: "// @@@ If the bit index is non-negative, then the bit at that index is set to false."

In method clear(int bitIndex). The method clears the bit if index >=0 and within wordsInUse; else returns early. The spec: "If the bit index is non-negative, then the bit at that index is set to false."

But note that method may return early if wordIndex >= wordsInUse, meaning bit was already false (or out of range). Still after method, the bit at that index should be false (i.e., get(bitIndex) == false). Also the precondition: bitIndex is non-negative. So we assert: bitIndex >= 0 => !this.get(bitIndex). However need to use \old? Not needed as after operation we want bit false. So assert bitIndex >= 0 => !this.get(bitIndex); But need to refer to method get defined in same class: this.get(bitIndex). So final code:

<code>assert bitIndex >= 0 => !this.get(bitIndex);</code>

